.TH RUNON 1 "2025-01-01" "runon 0.4.0" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
runon \- push files and run command on remote server
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B runon
[\fIOPTIONS\fR] [\fB\-\-\fR] [\fICOMMAND\fR...]
.br
If no command is specified, opens an interactive shell.
.SH DESCRIPTION
\fBrunon\fR is a utility for pushing files to a remote server and executing commands
on it. It uses \fBpush-to\fR to sync files and then connects via SSH to run commands
or open an interactive shell. The tool remembers the last used connection parameters
(host, port, user, directory) from a history file for convenience.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
\fB\-h\fR, \fB\-\-host\fR \fIHOST\fR
Remote host (default: last used or example.com).
.TP
\fB\-p\fR, \fB\-\-port\fR \fIPORT\fR
SSH port (default: last used or 22).
.TP
\fB\-u\fR, \fB\-\-user\fR \fIUSER\fR
Remote user (default: last used or qe2).
.TP
\fB\-P\fR, \fB\-\-password\fR \fIPASS\fR
SSH password (for rsync/sshpass).
.TP
\fB\-i\fR, \fB\-\-identity\fR \fIFILE\fR
SSH identity file.
.TP
\fB\-d\fR, \fB\-\-dir\fR \fIDIR\fR
Remote directory (default: last used or .).
.TP
\fB\-X\fR, \fB\-\-no-x11\fR
Disable X11 forwarding.
.TP
\fB\-q\fR, \fB\-\-quiet\fR
Reduce verbosity.
.TP
\fB\-v\fR, \fB\-\-verbose\fR
Increase verbosity.
.TP
\fB\-h\fR, \fB\-\-help\fR
Display help message and exit.
.TP
\fB\-\-version\fR
Display version information and exit.
.SH HISTORY
\fBrunon\fR maintains a history file at \fI~/.cache/runon/history\fR that stores
information about the last connection. The format is:
.PP
.RS
timestamp:host:port:user:dir:exitvalue:cmdline
.RE
.PP
When options are not specified, \fBrunon\fR uses the values from the most recent
history entry. This allows you to quickly reconnect to the same server without
retyping connection parameters.
.SH WORKFLOW
The execution process follows these steps:
.IP 1. 4
Load last used connection parameters from history file (if available)
.IP 2. 4
Push files to remote server using \fBpush-to\fR with the specified options
.IP 3. 4
Connect via SSH and execute the command using \fI<dir>/scripts/run-cmd\fR
.IP 4. 4
If no command is specified, opens an interactive shell
.IP 5. 4
Record the execution in the history file
.SH EXAMPLES
.TP
Run a command on the default server:
.B runon ls -la
.TP
Connect to a specific host and run a command:
.B runon -h myserver.com -u deploy "cd /var/www && ls"
.TP
Open an interactive shell on a remote server:
.B runon -h myserver.com -u deploy -d /var/www
.TP
Run a command with custom port and identity file:
.B runon -h myserver.com -p 2222 -i ~/.ssh/custom_key "systemctl status nginx"
.TP
Push files and run command with password authentication:
.B runon -h myserver.com -P mypassword "deploy.sh"
.TP
Disable X11 forwarding:
.B runon -X -h myserver.com "xterm"
.SH FILES
.TP
\fI~/.cache/runon/history\fR
History file storing last used connection parameters and command executions.
